# Help: The software RAID (MD) features md-raid leaves out
#
# Layered on storage/md-raid.config: clustered MD, which coordinates
# an array's nodes through the distributed lock manager, the lockless
# bitmap, and the KUnit tests of the RAID6 syndrome and XOR code
# RAID456 uses.
#
# Prerequisites inlined per the self-containment rule:
# - MD and BLK_DEV_MD, and MD_RAID456, which selects RAID6_PQ and
#   XOR_BLOCKS, the code the tests test.
# - DLM, on CONFIGFS_FS, for MD_CLUSTER.
# - KUNIT for the tests.
#
# Tristate, loaded on demand; no builtin/ counterpart needed.
# See: drivers/md/Kconfig
# See: lib/raid/Kconfig
# See: https://docs.kernel.org/driver-api/md/md-cluster.html

#
# Inlined prerequisites
#
CONFIG_MD=y
CONFIG_BLK_DEV_MD=m
CONFIG_MD_RAID456=m
CONFIG_CONFIGFS_FS=m
CONFIG_DLM=m
CONFIG_KUNIT=y

#
# MD's options and tests
#
CONFIG_MD_CLUSTER=m
CONFIG_MD_LLBITMAP=y
CONFIG_RAID6_PQ_KUNIT_TEST=m
CONFIG_XOR_KUNIT_TEST=m
